# Rule name: Module production UI layout


## Rule

New Age **business modules** share one **production UI layout** (sidebar shell, home
orange stage, inner page headers, spacing tokens). **Play is out of scope** — it uses
`play` → `playdoo` → `deesplay`, not this module shell.

Before creating or editing module **UI chrome** (shell, home/dashboard header, global
theme, login shell), read the reference implementation and align structure and tokens —
do not invent a parallel layout (e.g. React + Tailwind dashboard, dark sidebar, extra
page gutters).

### Scope — applies when

- The repository has a filled **`docs/module.yaml`** (business module), **or**
- Paths under **`frontend-web/`**, module **`components/AppShell.vue`** (or
  `components/layout/AppShell.vue`), module **home/dashboard** views, module
  **`assets/theme.css`** / global layout CSS, **DeepiKiosk** `views/*.ejs` +
  `public/deepi.css`.

### Scope — does not apply

- **`play`**, **`playdoo`**, standalone **`deesplay`** (design system only).
- **`auth-service/frontend`** (ACL admin — not a product module shell).
- **`helm-charts`**, **`contracts`**, **`platform-api`**, backends without UI.
- Legacy **`frontend/`** (non–`frontend-web`) in a module — **do not extend**; migrate
  or leave deprecated unless explicitly asked.

### Reference (canonical)

| Role | Location |
|------|----------|
| **Primary reference** | `deepivoice/frontend-web` — `AppShell.vue`, `HomeView.vue`, `assets/theme.css` |
| **Documented parity** | `deepiflow/frontend-web/docs/deepivoice-layout-parity.md` (Flow ↔ Voice; reuse tokens for other modules) |
| **Non-Vue module** | `deepikiosk` — same semantics in `public/deepi.css` (`.dv-*`), `views/home.ejs`; Cursor rule `no-display-font.mdc` |

When two modules disagree, **DeepiVoice** wins for shell/home structure unless the user
names an approved product exception in the task.

### Stack

- Production client = **`frontend-web/`**: Vue 3 + TypeScript + Vite + Vuetify +
  **`@deepidoo/deesplay`** (theme **LIGHT**, `globals.scss`, `Deepi*` primitives).
- **Typography**: **Inter only** (`400–700` weights in `index.html`). No Syne or other
  display/geometric fonts in module UI, email, or comments.
- Do **not** use **`DeepiDashboard`** (Play widget board) for module home/shell — module
  home uses the **`.stage`** pattern below, not the dashboard grid component.

### Application shell

- Sidebar width **`248px`** (`--sidebar-w` or equivalent).
- Main content padding: **`1.35rem 1.5rem 2rem`** (top / horizontal / bottom).
- Mobile (≈ **`max-width: 900px`**): main **`1rem`**, bottom nav if the reference module uses it.
- **No extra horizontal gutters** in views (no ad-hoc `40px` page margins) — lateral
  spacing comes from the shell only.
- Wordmark: **`Deepi<span class="brand-{module}">Name</span>`** in sidebar (class name
  matches module branding, e.g. `brand-voice`, `brand-flow`, `brand-ads`).

Wrap routed content in **`AppShell`** (or Kiosk equivalent); routes like `/login` and
player fullscreen may use **`bare`** / no shell — follow the reference module.

### Home / dashboard (orange stage)

Use the **same DOM skeleton** as DeepiVoice `HomeView.vue`:

```html
<div class="home | page-stack page-stack--home">  <!-- column; gap 1.75rem -->
  <header class="stage">
    <div class="stage-glow" aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="stage-grid" aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="stage-copy">
      <p class="kicker">Deepi<span class="brand-*">Module</span></p>
      <h1>…</h1>
      <p class="lede">…</p>
    </div>
    <div class="stage-viz">… module-specific viz …</div>
  </header>
  <section class="tiles | …">…</section>
</div>
```

Stage tokens (match reference CSS):

| Token | Value |
|-------|--------|
| `min-height` | `clamp(240px, 32vh, 340px)` |
| `padding` | `clamp(1.5rem, 3.5vw, 2.5rem) clamp(1.35rem, 3vw, 2.25rem)` |
| `border-radius` | `20px` |
| Column gap | `1.5rem` |

Module-specific content belongs in **`.stage-viz`** and tiles — not a different header
pattern.

### Inner pages (no orange stage)

```html
<div class="page-stack | vault">   <!-- gap 1.25rem -->
  <header class="hero-head">       <!-- padding-top 0.4rem -->
    <p class="kicker">…</p>
    <h1>…</h1>
    <p class="lede">…</p>
  </header>
  …
</div>
```

Shared typography classes (from module `theme.css` / reference):

- **`.kicker`**: ~0.72rem, uppercase, letter-spacing ~0.18em
- **`.lede`**: ~0.95rem, margin-top ~0.7rem
- **`.hero-head h1` / `.stage h1`**: Inter, weight 700, no arbitrary display font

### Buttons (filters / primary)

Align with DeepiVoice `theme.css`: secondary `.btn` (min-height 32px, radius 8px);
`.btn-primary` pill (min-height 40px); hover primary uses **primary-700**, not lift-only
effects unless reference module does.

### Docker / local dev

Module UI for humans = **`frontend-web`** (Vue). Do not point compose/README “UI” at
legacy **`frontend/`** (React) for New Age module work unless the user explicitly maintains
that stack.

### Product exceptions

Document in code when intentionally diverging (e.g. DeepiFlow floating search on
Discover, mini-player, immersive routes). **Do not** treat exceptions as a new global layout.

### Agent checklist (before finishing UI work)

1. Confirmed repo is a **module** (`docs/module.yaml`), not **Play**.
2. Shell spacing and sidebar match reference (248px / 1.35rem / 1.5rem).
3. Home uses **`.stage`** tree; inner pages use **`.hero-head`** + **`.page-stack`**.
4. **Inter** only; Deesplay LIGHT theme wired.
5. No new parallel UI library or legacy React shell for production module paths.
